{"step_index":37,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T13:41:11Z","content":"Now the hackathon-winning README (15 marks for Checkpoint 1):","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"# NEURAX 3.0 — Visual Inspection & Defect Root-Cause Assistant\n\n> **NEURAX HACKATHON 3.0 · Domain 2 — AI in Industry & Automation**\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Problem Understanding\n\nHigh-throughput manufacturing environments face compounding losses from three interlocking problems that generic tools treat in isolation:\n\n| Problem | Consequence |\n|---|---|\n| Subtle defects missed at production speed | Escapes → warranty claims, recalls |\n| Bottlenecks undetected in multi-station flow | Lost throughput, idle WIP, overtime cost |\n| No connection between quality and process conditions | Root causes never addressed; defects recur |\n\nNEURAX 3.0 is a **unified industrial decision-support system** that solves all three simultaneously — without requiring live hardware, PLC connections or robotic integration.\n\n---\n\n## 🏗️ Architecture\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                       NEURAX 3.0 System                         │\n│                                                                 │\n│  ┌──────────────┐    ┌──────────────────┐    ┌──────────────┐  │\n│  │  Image Input  │    │ Production CSVs  │    │  Economic    │  │\n│  │  (JPG/PNG)   │    │  (Arena Sim)     │    │  Parameters  │  │\n│  └──────┬───────┘    └────────┬─────────┘    └──────┬───────┘  │\n│         │                     │                      │          │\n│  ┌──────▼───────┐    ┌────────▼─────────┐            │          │\n│  │  YOLOv8      │    │  Production      │            │          │\n│  │  Inference   │    │  Analyser (TOC)  │            │          │\n│  │  Engine      │    │                  │            │          │\n│  └──────┬───────┘    └────────┬─────────┘            │          │\n│         │                     │                      │          │\n│  ┌──────▼───────┐    ┌────────▼─────────┐            │          │\n│  │  Defect      │    │  Bottleneck      │            │          │\n│  │  Registry    │    │  Detector        │            │          │\n│  │  + Drift     │    │  + WIP Estimate  │            │          │\n│  └──────┬───────┘    └────────┬─────────┘            │          │\n│         │                     │                      │          │\n│         └──────────┬──────────┘                      │          │\n│                    │                                  │          │\n│           ┌────────▼─────────┐              ┌────────▼───────┐  │\n│           │  Root-Cause      │              │  Profitability │  │\n│           │  Correlator      │◄─────────────│  Engine        │  │\n│           │  (Rule Engine)   │              │  (What-If Sim) │  │\n│           └────────┬─────────┘              └────────────────┘  │\n│                    │                                             │\n│           ┌────────▼──────────────────────────────────────────┐ │\n│           │          Streamlit Dashboard (4 Tabs)              │ │\n│           │  Quality │ Flow │ Root Cause │ Profitability       │ │\n│           └───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Data Sources\n| Dataset | Description |\n|---|---|\n| Product images | Surface defect images (crack, hole, rust, scratch, normal) |\n| `Model 1.csv` | 10-feature baseline sequential line (Arena simulation) |\n| `Model 2.csv` | 16-feature variable demand & shift dynamics |\n| `Model 3.csv` | 77-feature complex multi-line & SKU routing |\n| `ParametersFile.xls` | Simulation input parameters |\n\n---\n\n## 🔬 Approach\n\n### 1. Defect Detection & Localisation (YOLOv8)\n- **Model**: YOLOv8 trained on 5 classes — `crack`, `hole`, `rust`, `scratch`, `normal`\n- **Modes**: Handles both detection (bounding boxes) and classification (softmax) model outputs\n- **Uncertainty Handling**:\n  - `confidence ≥ 0.45` → hard classification (PASS / DEFECT)\n  - `0.25 ≤ confidence < 0.45` → **UNCERTAIN** (flag for human review)\n  - `confidence < 0.25` → **NOVEL** (possible new defect type, flag for human review)\n- **Annotation**: Colour-coded bounding boxes + confidence score + status badge\n\n### 2. Bottleneck Detection (Theory of Constraints)\n- Reads Rockwell Arena simulation CSVs (station utilisation, waiting times, parts counts)\n- Identifies the **system constraint** as the station with maximum utilisation\n- Quantifies:\n  - Throughput gap (demand − actual parts)\n  - WIP buildup using **Little's Law** (WIP = λ × W)\n  - Bottleneck idle cost vs capacity\n\n### 3. Root-Cause Correlation (Rule Engine)\n- Deterministic correlation rules map process conditions → probable defect causes:\n  - `Drilling Util > 85%` + `crack/scratch` → Tool vibration / wear\n  - `Milling Util > 85%` + `crack/scratch` → Thermal stress / coolant issue\n  - `Assembly Util > 85%` + `scratch/hole` → Rushed handling\n  - `Assembly Waiting Time > 50 min` + `rust/scratch` → Surface degradation in WIP queue\n- **Batch drift detection**: Rolling 3-unit window defect rate with slope analysis\n- Each card shows: Evidence → Probable Cause → Recommended Action → Confidence\n\n### 4. Profitability Estimation (Economic Model)\n- No cost data in CSVs → user-configurable sliders\n- Financial components:\n  ```\n  Gross Revenue     = Good Units × (Scrap Cost × Revenue Multiplier)\n  Scrap Loss        = Defect Units × Scrap Cost per Unit\n  Idle Loss         = Bottleneck Wait Time × Downtime Cost/min\n  Opportunity Loss  = Throughput Gap × Unit Revenue\n  Net Margin        = Gross Revenue − All Losses\n  ```\n- **What-if simulator**: Sliders for bottleneck reduction % and scrap reduction % → instant margin projection\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 Quick Start\n\n### Prerequisites\n```bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n### Place model weights\n```\nD:\\acceleration\\best.pt     ← primary location (auto-detected)\n```\n\n### Run\n```bash\nstreamlit run app.py\n```\n\n### Using the App\n1. **Tab 1 — Quality Inspection**: Upload product images → click \"Run Inspection\" → see annotated defect localisation\n2. **Tab 2 — Production Flow**: CSVs auto-loaded from `D:\\acceleration\\` or upload via sidebar → see bottleneck highlighted\n3. **Tab 3 — Root Cause**: Select a model → see evidence-based causal chain between process conditions and defects\n4. **Tab 4 — Profitability**: Adjust cost sliders → see financial waterfall → use what-if simulator\n\n---\n\n## 📁 Project Structure\n\n```\nneurax_app/\n├── app.py                          ← Streamlit main application (4 tabs)\n├── requirements.txt\n├── modules/\n│   ├── defect_detector.py          ← YOLOv8 wrapper, uncertainty handling\n│   ├── defect_registry.py          ← Session-scoped per-unit results store\n│   ├── production_analyzer.py      ← TOC bottleneck + WIP + throughput KPIs\n│   ├── root_cause.py               ← Rule-based correlation + drift analysis\n│   └── profitability.py            ← Financial model + what-if simulator\n├── utils/\n│   ├── constants.py                ← Classes, thresholds, correlation rules\n│   └── chart_helpers.py            ← Plotly chart factory (all visualisations)\n└── README.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🏆 Judging Criteria Coverage\n\n| Criterion | How Addressed |\n|---|---|\n| Defect detection accuracy | YOLOv8 with 5 trained classes, confidence thresholds |\n| Defect localisation | Bounding boxes in detection mode; class scores in classification |\n| Robustness to unseen conditions | UNCERTAIN + NOVEL flags instead of forced misclassification |\n| False-reject / false-accept | Adjustable confidence threshold slider |\n| Root-cause correlation | Rule engine with HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW evidence cards |\n| Explainability | Each card shows Evidence → Cause → Action chain |\n| Technical implementation | Modular, all pure Python, reproducible |\n| UI/UX & Visualisation | 4-tab Streamlit, Plotly charts, colour-coded status |\n\n---\n\n## 🛠️ Tech Stack\n\n| Component | Technology |\n|---|---|\n| AI / Vision | Ultralytics YOLOv8 |\n| UI | Streamlit 1.35+ |\n| Visualisation | Plotly Express + Graph Objects |\n| Data Processing | pandas, numpy |\n| Image Processing | PIL (Pillow), OpenCV (via ultralytics) |\n| Production Analysis | Custom TOC engine (pure Python) |\n\n---\n\n*NEURAX 3.0 — All analyses are advisory/simulated. No live hardware access required or used.*\n","Description":"Comprehensive hackathon README covering problem understanding, architecture, approach, and judging criteria mapping","Overwrite":false,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\win-10\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\neurax_app\\README.md","toolAction":"Creating README","toolSummary":"Hackathon README file"}}]}
