{"step_index":39,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T13:41:55Z","content":"{{ CHECKPOINT 0 }}\n **The earlier parts of this conversation have been truncated due to its long length. The following content summarizes the truncated context so that you may continue your work. **\n\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. NEURAX HACKATHON 3.0\r\nDOMAIN 2 · AI IN INDUSTRY AND AUTOMATION\r\nProblem Statement: Visual Inspection & Defect Root-Cause Assistant\r\nDescription:\r\nHigh-throughput manufacturing lines are difficult to optimize because product quality, process capacity and economics interact. Defect signatures can be subtle and easy to miss at production speed, while bottlenecks may emerge from cycle-time imbalance, excess work-in-process, downtime, changeovers, low utilization, scrap or rework. For this challenge, teams should design for a realistic multi-stage manufacturing environment with mixed product variants, changing inspection conditions, recurring defect families, batch-to-batch process drift, varying station capacity and operating conditions that affect both throughput and profitability.\r\nThe objective is not to build another image classifier, generic labeling tool or isolated KPI dashboard. The objective is to build a unified industrial decision-support system that can explain what is wrong with a product, where \n<truncated 2519 bytes>\n2. 1. Where are your Excel / CSV files? (Filenames & Sample Rows)The operational datasets from the Rockwell Arena simulations are stored in your project root folder (D:\\acceleration\\):Filenames:Model 1.csv (10 features — baseline sequential line)Model 2.csv (16 features — variable demand & shift dynamics)Model 3.csv (77 features — complex multi-line & SKU routing)ParametersFile.xls (Simulation input parameters file)Sample Row (Model 1.csv):DemandTotal partsParts per hourAssembly Waiting TimeAssembly UtilDrilling Waiting TimeDrilling UtilMilling Waiting TimeMilling Util5004826097.20.98212.40.8218.10.4852. What are the exact YOLOv8 class names in your model?The target classes used by your dataset structure and best.pt model are:crackholenormal (or acceptable)rustscratch3. Where is your best.pt weights file located?Your trained YOLOv8 model weights file should be downloaded from Google Colab and placed directly in your project root folder:Primary Location: D:\\acceleration\\best.ptFallback Location (if train\n<truncated 785 bytes>\n\n# Previous Session Summary:\n# NEURAX 3.0 — Session Continuation Summary\n\n---\n\n## 1. Outstanding User Requests\n\n### IMPLEMENTATION — Copy project to D:\\acceleration and run the app\n- **Status**: IMPLEMENTATION (partially complete — all files written to scratch, but NOT yet copied to `D:\\acceleration\\` or tested)\n- The user's actual project root is `D:\\acceleration\\`. The app needs to be placed there and verified with `streamlit run app.py`.\n\n### NOT STARTED — Verify app runs without errors\n- The app has been built but **not yet launched or tested**. No `pip install` or `streamlit run` was executed. Syntax errors may exist.\n\n### NOT STARTED — Integration with existing training artifacts\n- The user has `D:\\acceleration\\best.pt` and the 3 CSV files. The app auto-detects these paths but this has not been verified in a live run.\n\n---\n\n## 2. User Knowledge\n\n### Dataset details (verbatim from user):\n> \"Model 1.csv (10 features — baseline sequential line), Model 2.csv (16 features — variable demand & shift dynamics), Model 3.csv (77 features — complex multi-line & SKU routing), ParametersFile.xls (Simulation input parameters file)\"\n\n> Sample Row (Model 1.csv): `Demand=500, Total parts=482, Parts per hour=60, Assembly Waiting Time=97.2, Assembly Util=0.982, Drilling Waiting Time=12.4, Drilling Util=0.821, Milling Waiting Time=8.1, Milling Util=0.485`\n\n### YOLOv8 class names (verbatim):\n> \"crack, hole, normal (or