{"step_index":77,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T14:16:14Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Walkthrough documenting the completed NEURAX 3.0 system, including architecture, how to run the Streamlit app, model integration, dataset loading, and hackathon evaluation checklist.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Walkthrough: NEURAX 3.0 Industrial Decision-Support System\n\nWe have designed, coded, and assembled the complete **NEURAX 3.0** system for **NEURAX Hackathon 3.0 (Domain 2: AI in Industry & Automation)**.\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 How to Run the Application\n\nNavigate to the project folder and launch Streamlit:\n\n```powershell\ncd C:\\Users\\win-10\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\neurax_app\npython -m streamlit run app.py\n```\n\n---\n\n## 📂 Project Architecture & File Structure\n\n```\nneurax_app/\n├── app.py                          # Main Streamlit 4-Tab Web Application\n├── requirements.txt                # Dependencies (streamlit, ultralytics, plotly, etc.)\n├── README.md                       # Comprehensive Checkpoint 1 (15 Marks) Submission Doc\n├── modules/\n│   ├── defect_detector.py          # YOLOv8 inference wrapper, bounding boxes & UNCERTAIN/NOVEL filter\n│   ├── defect_registry.py          # Session data store & rolling defect rate drift calculator\n│   ├── production_analyzer.py      # Theory of Constraints (TOC) engine & Little's Law WIP estimator\n│   ├── root_cause.py               # Evidence-based causal correlation rules engine\n│   └── profitability.py            # Economic model, loss waterfall & What-If scenario simulator\n└── utils/\n    ├── constants.py                # 5 target classes, thresholds, color mappings & causal rules\n    └── chart_helpers.py            # High-performance Plotly visualisations (waterfall, radar, donuts)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🛠️ Key Features Implemented\n\n### 1. 🔍 Quality Inspection (Tab 1)\n- **YOLOv8 Integration**: Automatically loads `D:\\acceleration\\best.pt` (with custom path override in sidebar).\n- **Target Classes**: `crack`, `hole`, `rust`, `scratch`, `normal`.\n- **False-Reject & Uncertainty Guard**:\n  - `Confidence >= 0.45`: Standard classified output (Pass / Defect).\n  - `0.25 <= Confidence < 0.45`: Flagged as **UNCERTAIN** for human verification.\n  - `Confidence < 0.25`: Flagged as **NOVEL** defect pattern.\n- **Visual Evidence**: Colored bounding boxes, confidence overlays, and status badges.\n\n### 2. 🏭 Production Flow Health (Tab 2)\n- **Simulation CSV Ingestion**: Supports `Model 1.csv`, `Model 2.csv`, `Model 3.csv` from `D:\\acceleration\\`.\n- **Theory of Constraints (TOC)**: Automatically identifies the bottleneck station across Drilling, Milling, and Assembly.\n- **WIP Estimation**: Uses Little's Law ($WIP = \\lambda \\times W$) to estimate bottleneck queue accumulation.\n- **Multi-Model Comparison**: Interactive radar and comparison charts comparing line capacities and idle times.\n\n### 3. 🔎 Root Cause Analysis (Tab 3)\n- **Evidence-Based Links**: Maps station overutilization and extreme wait times to physical defect types (e.g., Drilling overload $\\rightarrow$ tool wear/vibration micro-cracks; Assembly buffer delays $\\rightarrow$ surface oxidation/scratching).\n- **Process Drift Detection**: Computes rolling defect rates and detects rising/improving defect trends over time.\n\n### 4. 💰 Profitability & What-If Simulator (Tab 4)\n- **Financial Waterfall**: Converts operational numbers into Gross Revenue, Scrap Loss, Bottleneck Idle Cost, Opportunity Loss, and Net Margin.\n- **Interactive Sliders**:\n  - Scrap Material Cost (\\$)\n  - Line Downtime Cost (\\$/min)\n- **What-If ROI Calculator**: Interactive sliders for bottleneck reduction and scrap reduction with instant profit uplift projection.\n- **Executive Export**: Downloadable markdown analysis summary report.\n","Description":"Walkthrough artifact for the complete NEURAX 3.0 